From: Felix <52862870+devilAPI@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:08:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 53/53] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8996: DDR bandwidth for the GPU
 OPPs

The GPU node has a gfx-mem interconnect path, but its OPPs carry no
bandwidth, so the GPU never votes for DDR (mas_oxili 0/0 in
interconnect_summary). DDR then runs at what the display alone asks for
(about 3.4 GB/s average, a quarter of msm8996's LPDDR4), and the a530
renders and Android composes on the GPU with a starved memory bus.

Give each OPP a peak vote, the top one the full DDR bandwidth (14.4 GB/s,
1804.8 MHz x 8 bytes) as the downstream bus table did at the top GPU
level. msm_gpu drops to the lowest OPP when idle, so the vote falls to
1.6 GB/s between frames.

ZTE Axon 7, LineageOS 24 animations (gfxinfo janky frames, with the
QSEED2 scaler patch): ripple + open/back 34 -> 19 %, notification shade
22 -> 17 %, launcher drawer 7 -> 3 %, app open to home 13 -> 11 %.

Ported from the LineageOS 24 kernel series (same mainline 7.3.1 base).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FVN6i49UMoL3MhGT7nwMzG
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996.dtsi | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996.dtsi
index d8412567d..c82482b48 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996.dtsi
@@ -1305,30 +1305,37 @@ gpu_opp_table: opp-table {
 				 */
 				opp-624000000 {
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <624000000>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <14400000>;
 					opp-supported-hw = <0x09>;
 				};
 				opp-560000000 {
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <560000000>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <11200000>;
 					opp-supported-hw = <0x0d>;
 				};
 				opp-510000000 {
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <510000000>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <9600000>;
 					opp-supported-hw = <0xff>;
 				};
 				opp-401800000 {
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <401800000>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <7200000>;
 					opp-supported-hw = <0xff>;
 				};
 				opp-315000000 {
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <315000000>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <5600000>;
 					opp-supported-hw = <0xff>;
 				};
 				opp-214000000 {
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <214000000>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <3200000>;
 					opp-supported-hw = <0xff>;
 				};
 				opp-133000000 {
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <133000000>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <1600000>;
 					opp-supported-hw = <0xff>;
 				};
 			};
